{"item": "T-0026", "job": "adjudicate-t-0026", "kind": "ruling", "product": "asf", "text": "What was disputed is whether make_worktree's push-gate call should be unconditional or should skip itself when asf.hooks.ensure_git_hooks is absent — the working tree held an uncommitted softening to getattr(hooks, 'ensure_git_hooks', None), and the branch was held three times because no session would commit it. The softening is OVERRULED and has been reverted: it is fail-open on the one gate this item exists to install, and it contradicts both the item's own title and D10 as the plan states it at line 341, \"no path may reach git worktree add without the hooks in place\"; it bought a green suite by deleting the feature, and it does not come back in a later round. The unconditional call at asf/workers/spawn.py:160 is UPHELD exactly as committed in 16c99bd, which is plan step 1 verbatim. What now holds is that the stalemate was never a code-design question at all: asf/hooks.py has no ensure_git_hooks, and docs/plans/f-0075.md:15,17 queue Task 8354 behind Task 8353 precisely because 8353 creates it — T-0026 was launched out of order, so the six test_sample_product failures are the dependency's absence, not a defect in this diff, and I confirmed this by running both variants. What changes is that no further correction round is spent on spawn.py: the branch stands as pushed, it is expected to be red until Task 8353 lands, and the remaining work is a sequencing decision that belongs to the operator, since fail-closed and a green suite are mutually exclusive on this branch and no edit inside T-0026's footprint can reconcile them without abandoning D10.\nNEEDS OPERATOR: Task 8353 (F-0075, asf/hooks.py — ensure_git_hooks) must land before T-0026 merges — land 8353, then rebase task/T-0026 onto it and re-run the gate; do not merge T-0026 first.", "ts": "2026-09-22T18:36:04Z"}
